; CoreLR command test: watch the machine react
; Stays inside 200 x 200 mm, centre = origin.
; Start: pen up, back to the origin.
M5
G90 G0 X0 Y0
G21 G17 G54 G94
; -- 1. Pen up/down: listen to the servo --
M3
M5
M3
M5
; -- 2. Axes, pen up (+Y = up the wall) --
G0 X50 Y0
G0 X-50 Y0
G0 X0 Y0
G0 X0 Y50
G0 X0 Y-50
G0 X0 Y0
; -- 3. Diagonals, pen up, to each corner --
G0 X100 Y100
G0 X-100 Y100
G0 X-100 Y-100
G0 X100 Y-100
G0 X0 Y0
; -- 4. A plus sign, pen down (G1) --
G0 X30 Y0
M3
G1 X-30 Y0
G1 X0 Y0
G1 X0 Y30
G1 X0 Y-30
G1 X0 Y0
M5
; -- 5. Relative mode: a 20 mm square --
G0 X-90 Y-20
M3
G91
G1 X20
G1 Y20
G1 X-20
G1 Y-20
G90
M5
; -- 6. Modal words, no spaces, lower case --
G0 X-80 Y60
M3
G1 X-60 Y80
X-40 Y60
x-20 y80
g1x0y60
N50 G1 X20 Y80 F1500 S0
M5
; -- 7. Comments of both kinds --
G0 X40 Y60
M3 (pen down) ; and a comment
G1 X60 (inline) Y80 ; tail
G1 X80 Y60

G1 X100 Y80
M5
; -- 8. G2 clockwise circle, R=25 --
G0 X-75 Y-60
M3
G2 X-25 Y-60 I25 J0
G2 X-75 Y-60 I-25 J0
M5
; -- 9. G3 counter-clockwise circle --
G0 X25 Y-60
M3
G3 X75 Y-60 I25 J0
G3 X25 Y-60 I-25 J0
M5
; -- 10. Full circles in one line --
G0 X10 Y-60
M3
G3 X10 Y-60 I-10 J0
M5
G0 X10 Y-90
M3
G2 X10 Y-90 I-10 J0
M5
; -- 11. Back to the origin, program end --
M5
G0 X0 Y0
M30
